    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [x] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [x] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n- [x] I have updated 'mini.nvim' to latest version of the `main` branch\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.snippets\n\n### Neovim version\n\n0.11.x\n\n### Description\n\nFirst, thanks for the great work, i've been really enjoying completion and pairs. I was trying to add snippets, but on multiple occasions i have tried deleting a snippet in the last line(s) (with dG or or any other motion that deletes the entire line) that still had placeholders free, which would then throw the error in the title, and delete/undo lines that weren't even affected by the snippet. \nMy interpretation is that the snippets marks for jumping to the placeholders can go out of range by deleting enough lines for them to reference non-existent lines (maybe even columns), which then triggers this problem. If there are enough lines for the references to make sense, no error, obviously. If you delete enough for it to go out of range -> placeholders in the last line, delete the entire line, or delete till the end of the file from anywhere, it fails.\n\n### Reproduction\n\nInstall mini from main, setup surround without any options, load snippets from global.json. Create any snippet in a new file. Exit insert, move above the line and dG, (works reliably, other motions like d2d sometimes work). \n\nI made a sample config that you can look at. I verified it working in there: \n\n[nvim_repro.tar.gz](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/22660583/nvim_repro.tar.gz)",
