            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Thanks for the issue!\n\n> ... on multiple occasions i have tried deleting a snippet in the last line(s) (with dG or or any other motion that deletes the entire line) that still had placeholders free ...\n\nThis is [not recommended](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/126ce3328c78399dcff58272f6f540a373b62a75/doc/mini-snippets.txt#L1105-L1110). Deleting region that doesn't contain tabstop ranges should be fine, but still do carefully. The reason for this is specifically to avoid situations like this, while accounting for it is not trivial.\n\nIn general, I'd suggest to explicitly stop snippet session (with `<C-c>` or by finishing going through the snippet before going into Normal mode) before doing such kind of editing.\n\n> Also the placeholders cannot be deleted or otherwise interacted with if you change the snippet\n\nDoing `<C-c>` should stop snippet session even in this case.\n\n---\n\nClosing as a documented limitation.",
